	)
	(text "48 V to 5 V synchronous buck: LM5116 (6-100 V input, emulated current mode) + 2 x BSC098N10NS5 (100 V, 9.8 mΩ).\nDesigned for 34-58 V in, 5.09 V out, 5 A, following the LM5116 datasheet (SNVS499) section 7.2.2.\nNOT yet simulated or built: review before layout.\n\nOutput voltage: Vout = 1.215 V x (1 + R119/R120) = 1.215 x (1 + 15k/4.7k) = 5.09 V. With 1 % resistors and the 1.6 % reference: 4.93 V to 5.25 V.\n    The CM5 input range is 4.75-5.25 V. Change R119/R120 to 0.1 % parts if the upper corner matters.\nFrequency: R117 12k: fsw = 1 / (12k x 284 pF + 450 ns) = 259 kHz. On-time at 58 V in is 340 ns (minimum about 100 ns).\nInductor: L3 10 uH, Isat 15.5 A. Ripple 1.76 A p-p at 48 V, 5.9 A peak at 5 A load.\nCurrent limit: R112 15 mΩ: 110 mV / 15 mΩ = 7.3 A peak (6.3 A min, 8.4 A max), sensed in the low-side source. R112 dissipates 0.34 W.\n    Route CS / CSG (U23 pins 12 / 13) as a Kelvin pair straight to the pads of R112. CSG and DEMB are tied to GND at R112.\n    TP55 / TP63 (CS) and TP64 / TP65 (GND) are for a four-wire measurement of R112: place all four at its pads.\nRamp: C101 = gm x L / (A x Rs) = 5 uA/V x 10 uH / (10 x 15 mΩ) = 333 pF, use 330 pF C0G.\nSoft start: C100 47 nF: 47 nF x 1.215 V / 10 uA = 5.7 ms.\nCompensation: Type II. Modulator gain = Rload / (A x Rs) = 1.02 Ω / 0.15 Ω = 6.8, with a pole at 1/(2π x 1.02 Ω x 224 uF) = 700 Hz.\n    R118/R119 = 3.1 gives a crossover near 14 kHz (fsw/18). Zero R118 x C102 at 1.25 kHz, C103 pole at 72 kHz.\nOutput caps: C105/C106 100 uF 10 V polymer (15 mΩ) + C107-C110 10 uF. About 224 uF effective.\nInput caps: C91-C97 2.2 uF 100 V X7S. Ripple current about 1.5 A rms at 5 A out. C90 (input sheet) is the bulk capacitor.\nGate drive: VCCX is grounded, so VCC = 7.4 V from V_IN. Gate charge 2 x 17 nC x 259 kHz = 9 mA (VCC limit 15 mA min).\n    U23 dissipates about 48 V x (5 mA + 9 mA) = 0.7 W: stitch the exposed pad into the ground plane with vias.\nBootstrap: D32 BAV21WS (250 V, 50 ns) + C99 1 uF between HB and SW.\nDiode emulation: DEMB grounded: the low-side FET turns off at zero current at light load, and the converter starts into a pre-biased output.\nUVLO: R114 + R115 = 360k, R116 13k: starts above (1.215 V / 13k - 5 uA) x 360k + 1.215 V = 33 V. Two 0603 resistors share the input voltage.\n    C104 1 uF sets the hiccup off-time (about 16 ms) after 256 cycles of current limit. D33 discharges C104 when V_IN drops.\nOn/off: SW1 grounds EN: the LM5116 shuts down to under 10 uA, plus 48 V / 330k = 0.15 mA through R113. D34 (15 V) keeps the EN node\n    within the rating of SW1 and of the test point. SW1 switches the 5 V rail only; the 48 V side of the board stays live.\nSnubber: R121 / C111 are not fitted. Add them if the SW node rings (start with 10 Ω + 470 pF) and re-check the losses.\nLayout: Keep the loop C91-C96 -> Q5 -> Q6 -> R112 -> C91-C96 as small as possible. SW copper only as large as the current needs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 35.56 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "02a85c8c-2081-4019-9281-de2771b6e478")
	)
